{"text": "Pohl Consumer Law Group - Bankruptcy Intake Summary\nPrepared by Nadia Rahimi, paralegal, for Everett Pohl. Intake interview\n06/02/2026. Internal file BK-26-0291.\n\nDebtor\nBAPTISTE-GREENE, LATOYA R. (goes by \"Toya\"). Born 17 Nov 1984. SSN 445 89\n7758. Kansas driver's license K04-71-9938. Lives at 1146 Poyntz Circle, Apt 3C,\nManhattan, KS 66502; renting since March 2024. Phone 785-555-0129, email\ntoya.bg84@inboxmail.example. Married, separated from her husband Marcus\nGreene, who is not filing. Two dependents, ages 9 and 13.\n\nEmployment and income\nParaprofessional at Flint Hills Unified School District 383 since 08/12/2019;\nemployee no. E-20714. Gross pay $2,684.00 per month over ten months. Receives\nchild support of $450 a month, irregularly. Mr. Greene is currently incarcerated at\nthe Riley County Jail, so do not count his income on Form 122A-1. She is below\nmedian for a household of three; no presumption of abuse.\n\nWhy she is filing\nWage garnishment by Sunflower Recovery Services LLC started May 15, 2026 on a\njudgment of $7,912.36 (Riley County District Court, Case No. 2025-LM-000847).\nMost of the unsecured debt is medical, from treatment for stage II breast cancer in\n2024 at St. Brendan Regional Medical Center, when she had no coverage for four\nmonths.\n\nDebts\nCreditor Account Balance\nTallgrass Bank ...4417 $18,204.11\nMeridian Auto MAF-2291077 $11,860.00\nSt. Brendan SB-00918824 $23,447.90\nSunflower judgment $7,912.36\nStudent loans 4 loans $31,250\n\nStudent loans are federal and will not be discharged; see 11 U.S.C. § 523(a)(8).\n\nAssets\nVehicle financed through Meridian Auto Finance Co.: 2019 compact SUV, VIN\n5NMS33AD7KH041926, Kansas plate 417 MTK, value about $9,500. She wants to\nreaffirm; payment is $318.74 a month. Checking and savings at Konza Federal\nCredit Union, member no. 0061-22804, combined balance $612.09 on the intake\ndate. Expects a tax refund of roughly 1,900 dollars. No real estate. Household\ngoods under exemption limits. Her grandmother's ring, appraised at $2,200, is\nexempt.\n\nPrior filings and other flags\n Prior Chapter 13 filed jointly with Marcus, Case No. 18-40662, dismissed\n10/04/2019 for missed plan payments. More than eight years is not required\nhere because the earlier case ended without a discharge.\n She transferred a 2011 pickup to her brother in Junction City in January 2026\nfor $1,000. Disclose on the statement of financial affairs.\n Credit counseling certificate no. 01356-KS-CC-039114477, completed 06/01/2026.\n\nNext steps\nFile the petition, Schedule I and Schedule J by June 19, 2026 to stop the\ngarnishment before the next pay date. Expect assignment to Judge Marchetti (Hon.\nEvelyn L. Marchetti) and a meeting of creditors under 11 U.S.C. § 341 about five\nweeks later. Fee: $1,450 plus the $338 filing fee; she paid $400 today by debit card\nending 9192. Mr. Pohl, Kan. S. Ct. No. 22715, to sign.", "kind": "PDF", "detail": "2 pages · 447 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Nadia Rahimi", "Everett Pohl", "BAPTISTE-GREENE", "LATOYA R.", "Marcus Greene", "Marcus", "Evelyn L. Marchetti", "Mr. Pohl"], "companies": ["Pohl Consumer Law Group", "Flint Hills Unified School District", "Sunflower Recovery Services LLC", "Tallgrass Bank", "Meridian Auto Finance Co.", "St. Brendan Regional Medical Center", "Konza Federal Credit Union", "Kan."]}, "topics": {"places": ["Manhattan", "KS", "Kansas", "Junction City"], "health": ["breast cancer", "treatment", "Stage II"], "sensitive": [], "names": ["Nadia", "Everett", "Marcus", "Marchetti", "Mr. Pohl", "Evelyn L."]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 76.89999999850988, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 29576.800000000745, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "post